  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn the spec for [the indexed setter for HTMLOptionsCollection](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/common-dom-interfaces.html#dom-htmloptionscollection-setter), it says this:\r\n> 5. If n is greater than or equal to zero, [append](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-append) value to the [select](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-elements.html#the-select-element) element. Otherwise, [replace](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-node-replace) the indexth element in the collection by value.\r\n\r\nAppending an element inserts it as a child, while replacing throws an exception if the child doesn't already have that parent. This creates inconsistent behaviour depending on whether the index is already used, and none of the browsers I checked actually throw in this case",
